the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the Alter of *a case* is *a number*; scenario element.
    the Geschäftsfähig of *a case* is *a truth value*; scenario element.
    Geschäftsfähigkeit holds for *a case*.
    Volljährigkeit holds for *a case*.
    Keine Entmündigung holds for *a case*.
    Volljährigkeit would hold for *a case*; unknown.

the knowledge base r4_5_pruefung_volljaehrigkeit includes:

the text of the_rulemap is at "sources/pruefung-volljaehrigkeit.ruml".

Geschäftsfähigkeit holds for a case if
    Volljährigkeit holds for the case
    and Keine Entmündigung holds for the case.

Volljährigkeit holds for a case if
    the Alter of the case is a number N
    and N >= 18.

% Where the expression has no result (a value it needs is missing), RUML's answer is undefined: the leaf holds only on the assumption below.
Volljährigkeit holds for a case if
    it is not the case that the Alter of the case is a number
    and Volljährigkeit would hold for the case.

Keine Entmündigung holds for a case if
    the Geschäftsfähig of the case is true.

